  "findings": [
    "Manual learned-spell commands validated membership but not current knowledge/stamina requirements. Recheck UI, authority admission and queued execution; retain slots and preserve item/script rules.",
    "Shoulder controls erased the soft target every frame and RT/A ignored it. Friendly spells default to self, X self-casts, D-pad cycles valid targets and A/RT honors that target without changing caster.",
    "The body-part ring mixed six aimed strikes with unrelated actions and narrow foot sectors. Six equal labelled sectors, D-pad navigation, hysteresis and neutral-on-open improve precise selection.",
    "Snapshot cadence used simulation delta; 2x sent more traffic. One ordered unreliable channel discarded older chunks for unrelated actors. Per-actor monotonic serials now reject stale data, and a wall-time deadline limits updates to 10 Hz.",
    "Loss of a final stopped-party state could leave the old walking animation until a staggered full refresh. Every periodic update now repeats party state.",
    "Full retained perception increased a Portal actor record to 3476 bytes. Sorted packed ID deltas, cached Zstandard compression and compatible legacy-array decoding reduce this stress-case record to 984 bytes without changing vision rules."
  ],
